WEBVTT

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:02.247
Hi, I'm Camellia!

00:00:02.247 --> 00:00:05.436
Here's how a street-view guessing game becomes a training ground.

00:00:08.975 --> 00:00:12.510
The idea: a guess is scored by its distance from the truth.

00:00:12.510 --> 00:00:14.278
Verifiable, with no judge to game.

00:00:17.758 --> 00:00:20.808
Each episode drops the model at a street panorama.

00:00:20.808 --> 00:00:22.163
One view, no metadata.

00:00:22.583 --> 00:00:25.119
It can look, zoom and move, at a small cost.

00:00:25.119 --> 00:00:27.909
A pin says what's at a spot, never whether it's close.

00:00:28.329 --> 00:00:30.036
Submit guess ends the episode.

00:00:30.036 --> 00:00:33.451
The score comes from the true distance, revealed only then.

00:00:33.871 --> 00:00:37.335
The trainer runs eight rollouts of one task, and nudges the LoRA

00:00:37.335 --> 00:00:38.490
toward the better ones.

00:00:40.483 --> 00:00:43.901
The game's curve subtracts cost, then floors at zero.

00:00:43.901 --> 00:00:49.219
Seventy-seven of two hundred replays scored exactly zero, near misses and wild ones alike.

00:00:49.639 --> 00:00:53.089
The trainer adds a slower decay and multiplies by cost, so

00:00:53.089 --> 00:00:54.343
bad guesses stay ordered.

00:00:56.192 --> 00:00:57.769
Now the part that looked like a bug.

00:00:58.192 --> 00:01:01.501
A rollout's advantage is its reward minus the group's mean,

00:01:01.921 --> 00:01:03.557
divided by the group's spread.

00:01:03.557 --> 00:01:07.812
With one task per step, that spread shrinks as the policy grows confident,

00:01:08.232 --> 00:01:10.878
so the same gap gets pushed about sixty times harder.

00:01:10.878 --> 00:01:13.259
Turning that off kept a fifth of the gain.

00:01:14.633 --> 00:01:18.917
Median error fell from twelve hundred twenty-six kilometres to six hundred sixty-two,

00:01:18.917 --> 00:01:22.844
as turns fell from six point seven to one point one.

00:01:23.975 --> 00:01:27.839
On this reward, the biggest win was not being catastrophically wrong, so

00:01:27.839 --> 00:01:30.414
the model learned to glance once and commit.

00:01:32.608 --> 00:01:36.768
To recap: tools that never hint, a reward that keeps bad guesses

00:01:36.768 --> 00:01:39.195
ordered, and a signal that amplifies itself.

00:01:39.615 --> 00:01:41.812
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:41.812 --> 00:01:42.439
I'm Camellia.

00:01:42.439 --> 00:01:42.753
Bye!
